 "notes": "AxionPhoton g_agamma from JWST NIRSpec blank-sky decaying-DM line search (Janish & Pinetti). Headline curve = Continuum Model 2sigma power-constrained limit, the lower (deepest-g) boundary of the red filled region in the bottom panel of Fig.2 (constraints.pdf in e-print), extracted as a vector figure. Calibrated on axis tick marks (bottom panel: y 10^-9=210.5px..10^-13=380.7px, 42.55px/dec; x 0.5eV=85.9px,1eV=218.1px,3eV=427.8px). Deepest point g=9.38e-12 GeV^-1 at m_a=2.15 eV reproduces the abstract value 9.4e-12 at 2.15 eV; at m_a=1 eV the spiky curve reaches ~2.4e-11 matching the quoted g>2.4e-11 (tau<2.4e26 s, verified via Gamma=g^2 m^3/64pi). The curve is intrinsically bin-by-bin spiky. The alternative Total Flux (black) bound is weaker (~1-2e-10) and not the headline. 2sigma power-constrained CL~0.95. Decaying-DM search: limit depends on the DM column not local density; NFW rho_s=0.18 GeV/cm^3, r_s=24 kpc, R_sun=8.1 kpc give D~7.5 GeV kpc/cm^3 for this line of sight (b=54.8,l=126) and implied local rho~0.3 GeV/cm^3 (recorded). Mass range ~0.8-2.5 eV.",
